* text=auto eol=lf

# Paradox script and localization are LF + UTF-8. The loc additionally needs a
# BOM, and so does every script .txt in this mod - `ck3.py validate` fails the
# build without one. NOTHING HERE PRESERVES A BOM: `text` governs line endings
# only, and a CRLF checkout would not strip a BOM either. The two are recorded
# together because they are checked together and are easy to conflate.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. The box this mod is written on has
# core.autocrlf=true, so without a declaration here every checkout writes CRLF
# into files the parent tooling repo declares LF. It went unnoticed because git
# cleans CRLF back to LF on the way in, which leaves `git status` clean over a
# working tree that is mixed - and it was mixed: two files under common/ had
# CRLF while the other twenty-three did not.
*.txt text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.gui text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.dds binary
*.tga binary
